Q: Deprecation warnings: in case (Qt::Key_A | Qt::SHIFT): A: <p><code>case</code> statements must use integral values that are known at compile-time, but <code>QKeyCombination::toCombined()</code> is a run-time method, so you can't use it in <code>case</code> statements. And you can't use variables for <code>case</code> statements, either.</p>
<p>Use <code>if</code>'s instead, as you already tried. But you don't need to use <code>toCombined()</code> in that situation, you can compare a <code>QKeyCombination</code> to another <code>QKeyCombination</code> directly, eg:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>if (key == (Qt::Key_A | Qt::ShiftModifier)){
    spdVal= (spdVal &lt; 10 * ssss) ? 0.0 : (spdVal - 10 * ssss);
} else if (key == (Qt::Key_S | Qt::ShiftModifier)){
    spdVal+= 10 * ssss;
}
</code></pre>
<p>As for the <code>QKeyCombination</code> constructor, you claim it accepts 2 parameters in either order, but there is no 2-param constructor that takes a <code>Qt::Key</code> as the <em>first</em> parameter, as you showed.  There are only two 2-param constructors, and the <code>Qt::Key</code> is the <em>second</em> parameter in both of them:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>QKeyCombination(Qt::KeyboardModifiers, Qt::Key)
QKeyCombination(Qt::Modifiers, Qt::Key)
</code></pre>
<p>For example:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>QKeyCombination keyA_keyShift = QKeyCombination(Qt::ShiftModifier,Qt::Key_A);
QKeyCombination keyS_keyShift = QKeyCombination(Qt::ShiftModifier,Qt::Key_S);
</code></pre>
<p>Where <code>Qt::ShiftModifier</code> is a <code>Qt::KeyboardModifier</code>.</p>

Q: Shift canvas contents to the left A: <p>If you want to move the whole contents you can use a copy global composite operation with a single drawImage(), drawing the canvas on itself. Doesn't appear to work in safari, but it is crazy fast in chrome.</p>
<pre><code>ctx.globalCompositeOperation = &quot;copy&quot;;
ctx.drawImage(ctx.canvas, -widthOfMove, 0);
// reset back to normal for subsequent operations.
ctx.globalCompositeOperation = &quot;source-over&quot;;
</code></pre>
